  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (basis recorded as cash); business-type activities accrual (measure net position), as FY2023/FY2024. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); business-type from the proprietary funds Total column (p6), Apartments Fund included. Fund balance roll-forward: 1,410,681 (as previously reported) + 437,953 - 325,790 + 195,346 - 110,706 - 153,299 (Debt Service Fund restatement) = 1,454,185. Business-type: 3,040,159 + 1,202,869 - 991,624 - 84,640 = 3,166,764. Charges for services 14,149 split: Park 5,634 (p13) + Cemetery 8,515 (Statement of Activities Cemetery care charges for services, p2), as FY2023. Proprietary cash flows (pp7-8) not recorded (not GAAP; as FY2023/FY2024). Cash: Total Governmental Funds cash and cash equivalents 741,621 and certificates of deposit 702,636 (p3); no prior-year balance sheet, so beginning cash null. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3; total assets 1,454,954 equals the p1 governmental column), business-type lines from p1; component unit excluded. Detail: General Fund from its budgetary comparison schedule (p9), because the General Fund departments combining statement is only partly in the trim (p13 shows General, Fire and Park; the Cemetery, Library and Community Building continuation page is not trimmed); Street Fund budget schedule (p10); Debt Service Fund budget schedule (p11) has no actual amounts, so no lines; nonmajor Keno, Sales Tax and Special funds (p12). No utility schedules, so no proprietary detail (as FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
